# EVERY fixture here must be ENUMERATED on the out-of-profile path, never
# silently dropped and never merely counted -- a dropped axiom is an incoherence
# the reasoner subsequently cannot see. Each yields non-empty coverage.omitted,
# so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent.
# #
# owl:topObjectProperty and owl:bottomObjectProperty -- built-in role
# semantics CR1-CR7 do not implement. Treated as an ordinary role, CR3 builds an
# edge for A subseteq EXISTS bottomObjectProperty.top and A is reported SATISFIABLE:
# a missed unsatisfiability, i.e. a FALSE PASS. Hence out-of-profile, not ignored.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
                     owl:onProperty owl:bottomObjectProperty ;
                     owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ] .
